<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord Chunshen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 238 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Huang Xie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lord Chunshen, personal name Huang Xie, was chief minister of the State of Chu for about twenty-five years under King Kaolie, and one of the Four Lords of the Warring States, famous for keeping thousands of retainers. He led Chu forces to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/handan">Handan</a> in 257 BCE and organised the last alliance against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 241 BCE. He was assassinated in 238 BCE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>, whose sister had become queen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lord-chunshen.jpg" alt="Lord Chunshen" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 冯梦龙、蔡元放 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%98%A5%E7%94%B3%E5%90%9B.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
